Overlay patch 0036: first-run onboarding prompts that actually appear.

The extractor's first prompt (Engine.cpp ShowYesNoBox "Please provide a ROM
/ extract into an O2R") and its error boxes (ShowMessage) are SDL message
boxes. Two platforms cannot use that:

- visionOS: an SDL message box cannot composite (it hangs the engine-thread
  nested runloop -> black screen). ShowYesNoBox returns IDYES immediately
  (straight to the SwiftUI ROM picker) and ShowMessage logs only.
- iOS, including LiveContainer: SDL builds the alert's UIWindow from
  UIScreen bounds and never sets windowScene. After the iOS 27 scene
  adoption that window is not on screen, so a fresh install blocks forever
  on a black screen and the O2R prompt never appears. LiveContainer only
  auto-attaches scene-less windows for apps that have NOT adopted scenes.
  ShowYesNoBox / ShowMessage call SohIos_AlertBlocking (shell) instead.

Desktop/oracle keep SDL. Needs <TargetConditionals.h> (added here).

Generate against a vendor tree with 0036 NOT applied (reverse it first).
The iOS branch lives in THIS patch, not a later one: a follow-on patch that
edits these same lines breaks apply-overlay's already-applied probe.


--- a/src/port/Engine.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Engine.cpp
@@ -813,9 +813,29 @@
 	return GameEngine::GetInterpolationFrameCount();
 }
 
+#include <TargetConditionals.h> // SOH_IOS (overlay 0036): TARGET_OS_VISION
+#if defined(__IOS__)
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0036): scene-attached first-run alert. SDL's message-box
+// window has no windowScene, so after the iOS 27 scene adoption it never
+// appears (black screen, no O2R prompt) on a normal install and inside
+// LiveContainer. cancelTitle == NULL is a single button; 1 = accept, 0 = cancel.
+extern "C" int SohIos_AlertBlocking(const char* title, const char* message, const char* acceptTitle,
+                                    const char* cancelTitle);
+#endif
 void GameEngine::ShowMessage(const char* title, const char* message, SDL_MessageBoxFlags type) {
 #if defined(__SWITCH__)
     SPDLOG_ERROR(message);
+#elif TARGET_OS_VISION
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0036): an SDL message box can't composite on visionOS
+    // (it hangs the engine-thread runloop -> black screen). Log only.
+    (void)title;
+    (void)type;
+    SPDLOG_ERROR(message);
+#elif defined(__IOS__)
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0036): see SohIos_AlertBlocking.
+    (void)type;
+    SohIos_AlertBlocking(title, message, "OK", nullptr);
+    SPDLOG_ERROR(message);
 #else
     SDL_ShowSimpleMessageBox(type, title, message, nullptr);
     SPDLOG_ERROR(message);
@@ -824,11 +844,22 @@
 
 int GameEngine::ShowYesNoBox(const char* title, const char* box) {
     int ret;
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#if TARGET_OS_VISION
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0036): no blocking SDL message box on visionOS — go
+    // straight to the SwiftUI ROM picker (SohIos_PickRomBlocking).
+    (void)title;
+    (void)ret;
+    SPDLOG_WARN(box);
+    return IDYES;
+#elif defined(_WIN32)
     ret = MessageBoxA(nullptr, box, title, MB_YESNO | MB_ICONQUESTION);
 #elif defined(__SWITCH__)
     SPDLOG_ERROR(box);
     return IDYES;
+#elif defined(__IOS__)
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0036): see SohIos_AlertBlocking. Yes -> IDYES.
+    (void)ret;
+    return SohIos_AlertBlocking(title, box, "Yes", "No") ? IDYES : IDNO;
 #else
     SDL_MessageBoxData boxData = { 0 };
     SDL_MessageBoxButtonData buttons[2] = { { 0 } };
